    put("toAccount", "12345")
    put("amount", 500.00)
}

apiClient.makeAuthenticatedRequest(
    "https://bank.com/api/transfers/send",
    "POST",
    transferData
)
```

**Why mobile apps don't need CSRF protection:**
- App explicitly constructs HTTP requests (not browser)
- No automatic credential inclusion
- Attacker cannot inject malicious code into installed app
- App-to-server communication is direct (no cross-origin requests)

